WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:03.320
Ask an AI to animate something,

00:03.320 --> 00:05.560
and it usually moves too fast.

00:05.560 --> 00:07.320
Everything happens at once,

00:07.320 --> 00:09.970
and nothing stays still long enough to read.

00:11.040 --> 00:13.850
Here is the same animation, slowed down.

00:14.080 --> 00:15.770
One change at a time.

00:16.000 --> 00:18.970
Each step holds, so you can follow it.

00:20.040 --> 00:21.810
This is the video skill,

00:21.960 --> 00:23.800
a free, open-source skill

00:23.800 --> 00:27.120
for coding agents like Claude Code and Codex.

00:27.120 --> 00:28.760
You ask for a video.

00:28.760 --> 00:30.680
Your agent writes the script,

00:30.680 --> 00:34.200
records the voice, and animates every frame in code,

00:34.200 --> 00:36.050
in time with the narrator.

00:37.120 --> 00:39.210
It makes three kinds of video.

00:39.440 --> 00:42.530
Explainers that draw how a system works.

00:42.560 --> 00:44.320
Walkthroughs of a real app,

00:44.320 --> 00:47.210
with a pointer that clicks as the narrator speaks.

00:47.440 --> 00:50.250
And motion loops for social posts.

00:51.320 --> 00:55.090
Every video follows the classic principles of animation.

00:55.160 --> 00:57.800
Then the agent checks its own work.

00:57.800 --> 00:59.520
It looks at every frame,

00:59.520 --> 01:01.730
and it measures every pause.

01:02.800 --> 01:05.760
Captions are included, in any language.

01:05.760 --> 01:07.680
No video editor needed.

01:07.680 --> 01:10.010
It's free, and the link is below.
